  "summary_en": "Legal analysis of cloud robotics, where physical robots integrate with cloud services. It maps the fragmented EU regulatory patchwork (product safety, liability, GDPR), discusses standards, multi-party liability attribution, and data protection issues such as controller identification, transparency and portability, and sets out an agenda for further research.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Cloud robotics is governed by a fragmented patchwork of EU product safety, liability, and data protection laws.",
   "The product/service distinction in EU product liability law is challenged by inseparable hardware-software-service mixtures.",
   "Balance needed between private standard-setting and public law-making.",
   "Attributing responsibility among multiple parties in cloud robotics ecosystems is difficult.",
   "Identifying controllers/processors, ensuring transparency and data portability are unclear in cloud robotics."
